Print the rect a window was asked for beside the one it got.

The setFrame trace said only that setFrame happened. A window that comes out the wrong size was
either ASKED for the wrong size or handed the right one and applied it badly, and those want
opposite work, so the trace could not start the investigation it existed for.

It answers immediately. iTerm2 Preferences opens far too short, and with both rects printed the
port is exonerated in one line:

  CIDER_WIN setFrame iTermPrefsPanel asked=924x539@332,-54 got=924x539@332,-54
  CIDER_WIN setFrame iTermPrefsPanel asked=689x141@332,344 got=689x141@332,344

The panel comes up at its nib size and the application itself then asks for 689x141. Every asked
equals its got, so setFrame is faithful and the wrong number is computed upstream.

WHERE IT COMES FROM, so the next attempt does not redo this.
-[PreferencePanel resizeWindowForTabViewItem:animated:] leads to
-[iTermPreferencesBaseViewController resizeWindowForCurrentTabAnimated:], which takes
[[[tabView selectedTabViewItem] view] subviews] firstObject and sizes the window to it. The tree
dump under CIDER_TRACE_VIEWS says what that view is:

  NSTabView              648x36 at 8,22
    NSView               644x8  at 2,2
      NSCustomView       0x0 at 0,0 mask=0x0 hidden=0 translates=0 cons=0

The pane is zero by zero. It is the only view in the whole panel with translates=0, it holds no
constraints, and the Preferences nib builds 4210 objects with not one NSLayoutConstraint among
them, so nothing in that nib uses auto layout at all. Something must size that view and nothing
does. Not the visual format API, which is implemented in Foundation NSLayoutConstraint.m and was
checked before being suspected.

This is the same shape as the MoneyMoney Preferences pane that never resizes and the two should be
taken together.

--- a/AppKit/NSWindow.m
+++ b/AppKit/NSWindow.m
@@ -1316,6 +1316,18 @@
         [self _animateWithContext: context];
         _CiderWindowNote("setFrame animate leave", self);
     }
+    /* THE RECT, because "setFrame leave" alone cannot say whether a window came out the wrong size
+     * because it was ASKED for the wrong size or because we applied the right one badly. iTerm2
+     * Preferences opens far too short and those two want opposite work. */
+    if (getenv("CIDER_TRACE_APP") != NULL) {
+        NSRect got = [self frame];
+
+        fprintf(stderr, "CIDER_WIN setFrame %s asked=%.0fx%.0f@%.0f,%.0f got=%.0fx%.0f@%.0f,%.0f\n",
+                object_getClassName(self),
+                newFrame.size.width, newFrame.size.height, newFrame.origin.x, newFrame.origin.y,
+                got.size.width, got.size.height, got.origin.x, got.origin.y);
+        fflush(stderr);
+    }
     _CiderWindowNote("setFrame leave", self);
     _CiderWindowStack("setFrame leave");
 }
